From c4a5d5760f786acd0224845c7d1313ea9d316c4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:56:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(title_bar): paint the bar with the window's own top
 edge

A server-side title bar could only use the palette colour, so it stood out
from applications that paint their own header. With
`[appearance.title_bar] color_source = "window"` it now mirrors the top five
logical pixels of the window it belongs to.

The bar is a scene buffer fed the client's committed buffer, the same way the
overview mirrors a card: committed damage, the explicit-sync acquire point,
the crop-aware source box and the surface's transform, so a screen-scaled or
rotated window still shows its own top edge. No pixels are read back, so the
bar costs a textured quad per frame and nothing per commit that does not
touch that edge. The palette colour stays painted underneath, which is what a
transparent top edge falls back to, and unfocused windows keep their colour
dimmed over the unfocused palette tone.

Because the bar can now be any colour, the title and the button symbols carry
a dark edge so they stay readable. Overview cards and close snapshots copy
the strip node too.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
