From 2bf8e4defce07f854dffc2654871e45d72e2f322 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:11:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] feat(title_bar): add an average colour mode

`color_source = "average"` paints the bar with the mean colour of the same
1-4 row strip instead of mirroring it, so the bar is one uniform colour and the
window's own title bar, tab row or loading indicator along that edge does not
read as fragments of itself inside it.

A mean cannot be taken without reading pixels back, so this mode finishes the
frame and reads the strip when the window repaints it, then keeps the result
until the edge changes: the flat colour is a single pixel stretched over the
bar, and no per-frame readback follows. Protected and external-only buffers
refuse the read, and the palette stays painted underneath as for the smear. The
colour is a plain sRGB value, so the surface's transfer function does not apply
to it.

Pins: three unit cases for the weighting (opaque mean, transparent pixels
contributing no hue, an empty or fully transparent strip), and a harness phase
whose client paints its edge green on one side and blue on the other - the
average must read the same blend at both ends, the smear the two sides.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
