From a45668fc896fad22af7d1f613428edd34dd40d18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:37:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] fix(title_bar): keep the average live, sRGB, and readable

Review of the average mode found that its cache compared the new mean with
itself, so the bar kept the first colour it was baked with for the frame's whole
life. Track the colour actually baked into the buffer instead.

A mode switch is not a commit, so `window` -> `average` never re-read the edge
and an idle window kept the palette, or the mean of an edge that had changed
while the bar was smearing. The mode the node was built for is now part of the
"redo the work" signal.

The bar also lost its contrast edge in average mode, although an average can be
any colour too; the title shadow and the symbol outline now cover both
window-derived modes. The flat colour is reset to sRGB rather than inheriting
the window's transfer function, and the readback asks for the format the
renderer prefers (decoding ARGB, ABGR and their opaque variants) instead of
assuming BGRA. The readback buffer is kept between commits.

The mean is computed from premultiplied pixels, so dividing by the alpha total
is the whole correction: weighting the components by alpha again made a
translucent edge render at half strength.

Pins: a semi-transparent unit case and an ABGR one; harness phases for a repaint
while averaging (fails with the frozen cache), for a live switch to average
after the edge changed while smearing (fails without the mode signal), and for
the mean following a repaint.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
